    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Ferroelectric-Materials-and-MEMS_REQ_0000081931": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar – Ferroelectric Materials and MEMS",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Materials Research Institute (MRI) at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a Postdoctoral Scholar to conduct interdisciplinary research on functional dielectric, piezoelectric, and ferroelectric materials for emerging memory and sensing applications.  The Postdoctoral Scholar will work collaboratively with Prof. Betul Akkopru-Akgun and Prof. Susan Trolier-McKinstry, contributing approximately equally to research activities in both groups. Under the direction of Prof. Betul Akkopru-Akgun, the Postdoctoral Scholar will investigate fluorite-type and wurtzite ferroelectrics for next-generation memory applications, focusing on the relationships between defect chemistry, intermediate switching states, polarization switching, fatigue, and retention. In collaboration with Prof. Trolier-McKinstry, the scholar will work on on fabrication of thin film and bulk single crystal microelectromechanical systems for multimodal sensing systems.  This will include design, fabrication, and testing of micro-electromechanical systems (MEMS) devices.  The successful candidate will have the opportunity to work at the intersection of functional materials, ferroelectrics, electrical characterization, microfabrication, and MEMS-based sensing, and will collaborate with researchers across multiple disciplines.  Required Qualifications  Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or a closely related field.  Demonstrated experience with electrical characterization of dielectric, piezoelectric, or ferroelectric materials.  Experience with techniques such as polarization–electric field (P–E) measurements, dielectric spectroscopy, leakage-current measurements, impedance spectroscopy, or related electrical characterization methods.  Strong experimental skills and experience with data analysis and interpretation.  Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research environment.  Preferred Qualifications  Experience with thin-film deposition and characterization.  Experience with MEMS design, fabrication, or testing.  Experience with microfabrication techniques, including lithography, etching, metallization, or related processes.  Experience with piezoelectric or ferroelectric devices for sensing, actuation, or memory applications.  Familiarity with bulk single-crystal materials and/or single-crystal MEMS.  Experience with device modeling or simulation  To apply, applicants should upload a cover letter detailing their qualifications for and interest in the position, a copy of their CV, and names and contact details (e-mail addresses and telephone numbers) for three references.    BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor_REQ_0000081356-2": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Materials Research Institute (MRI) at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a non-tenure-line Assistant Research Professor . The position will involve machine learning for autonomous thin-film materials synthesis, including representation learning for scientific data, multimodal data fusion, and real-time predictive modeling. This work will be performed as part of LATTICE (Layered and Thin Film Technologies with Intelligent Cloud Experimentation), a National Science Foundation Programmable Cloud Laboratory at The Pennsylvania State University's University Park campus.  The successful candidate will lead the development of specialized machine learning models that enable AI systems to interpret scientific data from instruments including atomic force microscopy, reflection high-energy electron diffraction, spectroscopic ellipsometry, X-ray diffraction, and similar characterization methods. These models serve as the perceptual layer for a multi-agent AI framework that will guide autonomous materials synthesis and interact with robotic systems. The models will be trained, calibrated, and validated against the specific data modalities produced by LATTICE instrumentation. The candidate will deploy these models on edge-computing infrastructure for real-time feedback during deposition and integrate them with the Lifetime Sample Tracking data platform. The position requires close collaboration with LATTICE domain scientists in thin-film growth and characterization, AI researchers developing the agentic workflow framework, and future users of the LATTICE framework. The candidate will also contribute to the scientific direction of the LATTICE ML/AI effort and mentor graduate students and postdoctoral scholars as appropriate.  Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or a related field, and should have postdoctoral or equivalent research experience demonstrating an independent record of publication in applied machine learning, computer vision, and/or scientific data analysis. Experience with one or more of the following is strongly preferred: deep learning for image analysis, multimodal or multi-task learning, or deployment of ML models in real-time or edge-computing environments. Domain knowledge of materials science, chemistry, or physics will be an advantage. Extensive programming experience in Python is required, and familiarity with PyTorch or JAX is preferred.  This is a non-tenure-line, limited-term appointment funded for one year from the date of hire with excellent possibility of renewal. To apply, applicants should upload a cover letter detailing their qualifications for and interest in the position, a copy of their CV, and names and contact details (e-mail addresses and telephone numbers) for three references. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.    BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor---Cocoziello-Digital-Twin_REQ_0000080944-2": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Professor - Cocoziello Digital Twin",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Cocoziello Institute of Real Estate Innovation at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a three-year Assistant Research Professor position with expertise in digital twins for the built environment (buildings and infrastructure), building information modeling, and data analytics for buildings. The position will be located on the University Park campus of Penn State. This position has a possible extension contingent on performance review and continued funding. The position has 60% research, 30% project management, and 10% research advising responsibilities. The successful candidate will manage the development of a robust digital twin effort, focusing on creating and implementing a digital twin strategy for the Penn State University Park campus. The candidate will collaborate with Institute faculty and industry partners, and guide graduate/undergraduate students on digital twin research and development activities. The successful candidate is expected to secure external funding for their research and disseminate research findings through peer-reviewed journals, conferences, and other effective channels. The individual should be highly motivated and knowledgeable of relevant literature, be able to lead their own individual projects, write grant proposals, and contribute to collaborative research efforts. Candidates should have: (1) an ability to manage and lead collaborative teams on research projects with significant industry engagement, (2) experience designing and/or adapting new technologies and techniques with a particular focus on digital twins and BIM related to the built environment, (3) strong written, visual, and oral communication skills, and (4) knowledge of human subject ethics and research procedures. Experience with industrialized construction, construction robotics, Virtual/Augmented Reality, and Artificial Intelligence is a plus. Qualifications A Ph.D. in Architectural Engineering, Civil Engineering, Architecture, or a related field is required. Applicants should provide evidence of strong potential for conducting and publishing research, competitiveness for external research funding, and excellence in communication across a range of audiences. Experience in industry-supported research activities is preferred. Selection Criteria Candidates will be evaluated on their potential to manage collaborative industry research projects, experience in research involving digital twins and Building Information Modeling, ability to secure external research funding, and ability to publish high-impact work. Applicants must submit the following: (1) a cover letter; (2) a complete CV; (3) a statement summarizing the applicant's philosophy and plan for pursuing successful research; and (4) contact information for three references. Applicants should address in their materials how they would contribute to creating/maintaining an inclusive and respectful work environment. System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. For more information about the position, please contact John Messner ( jim101@psu.edu ), Chair of the Search Committee. This is a term appointment, funded for three years from the date of hire, with an excellent possibility of renewal.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Teaching-Professor--Organization-Development-and-Change-_REQ_0000079398-2": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor (Organization Development and Change)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Learning & Performance Systems (LPS) invites applications for an Assistant Teaching Professor position to support its fully online master’s degree in Organization Development and Change (ODC) and other LPS programs, as needed. students to design and implement organization development and continuous improvement initiatives. Faculty in this role contribute to a collaborative instructional team and engage students in applied, globally informed coursework aligned with professional standards.  This non-tenure-line position is a 48-week faculty appointment, with the possibility of renewal and has primary responsibilities in teaching and graduate advising, as well as in supporting program administration. Faculty in LPS are part of a collegial, student-centered department that prioritizes strong teaching, thoughtful collaboration, and a positive, supportive work environment. Key Responsibilities Teach online, asynchronous courses in the fall, spring, and summer terms, with synchronous engagement for advising, webinars, and meetings; occasional in person teaching may be assigned. Coordinate with Penn State World Campus instructional designers and media specialists to ensure high‑quality online course development and delivery, accessibility/UDL, media integration, and continuous improvement; Advise master’s students including the master's in professional studies in Organization Development and Change, throughout the program, including capstone completion Advise online D.Ed. doctoral students, supporting progress through qualifying, comprehensive, and final examinations; course planning; and the development, implementation, and writing of the culminating capstone project. Includes annual participation in the 2–3 day Summer Summit residency held at the University Park campus; Support program administration activities including assisting with the course scheduling, program assessment and accreditation work, admissions review, orientation and community‑building for master’s students, onboarding of part‑time or new faculty, and student success initiatives; Collaborate and communicate effectively with the LPS department head, professor‑in‑charge of the WFED program, faculty colleagues, and department staff to support cohesive and responsive program operations; Participate in department and program meetings and events. Minimum Qualifications (Required) Earned doctorate (PhD or DEd) in education; workforce education and development; organization development and change; or a closely related field Evidence of excellence, or potential excellence, in online graduate teaching (asynchronous) and inclusive pedagogy Strong communication and collaboration skills Demonstrated strengths in time management, ability to prioritize multiple responsibilities, and organization Desired Qualifications Experience as an organization development and change or talent and development professional Familiarity with Canvas, online quality standards, and program assessment Experience designing or revising online courses in collaboration with instructional designers Understanding of the ethics surrounding the uses and integration of AI in higher education courses Evidence of student‑centered responsiveness including the ability to provide timely feedback and grading, respond promptly to working professionals, and manage multiple course deadlines in fast‑paced online environments Representative Teaching Portfolio ODC (examples): Appraising Organization Change and Development and Consulting; Implementing Training as an Organization Development Intervention; Marketing Organization Development; Project Management for Professionals; Lean‑Sigma for Professionals; Technologies for Work Effectiveness; Facilitating Organization Development and Change Through Technology; Leadership Competencies for Professionals Application Instructions Apply online at hr.psu.edu/careers and upload one PDF containing: a) Cover letter that clearly identifies the candidate’s qualifications related to the position; b) Curriculum vitae; c) Names and contact information for three professional references ; d) Teaching philosophy statement ( maximum two single‑spaced pages ) describing prior teaching and course design experience, ODC program alignment, relevant course expertise, and evidence of teaching effectiveness. Campus/Unit: College of Education — Department of Learning & Performance Systems (LPS), University Park, PA Appointment: Assistant Teaching Professor (non‑tenure-line), 48‑week; one year term with the possibility of renewal based on need, performance, and/or availability of funding. Full University benefits apply. Work Arrangement: In person preferred. The Department of Learning & Performance Systems is supportive of flexible (hybrid) work arrangements when aligned with the ability to meet the needs of the unit and the essential duties of the position. Questions related to flexible work should be directed to the department head during the interview process.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/College-of-Medicine/Adjunct-Associate-Professor_REQ_0000081980": {
      "title": "Adjunct Associate Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants .   JOB DESCRIPTION AND POSITION REQUIREMENTS Adjunct Associate Professor – Doctor of Public Health Program Department of Public Health Sciences, Penn State College of Medicine, Hershey, PA The Department of Public Health Sciences (PHS) at the Penn State College of Medicine invites applications for a Part-time Associate Professor position to provide leadership for the Doctor of Public Health (DrPH) program and support research activities within the department. The mission of PHS is to advance health through the design, conduct, and analysis of population-based biomedical research, the support of basic science and clinical research, the education of future generations of health professionals, and active engagement with the community to improve health and well-being. PHS comprises three academic divisions: Biostatistics and Bioinformatics, Epidemiology, and Health Services and Behavioral Research. The department offers graduate programs including the PhD in Epidemiology, PhD in Biostatistics, Doctor of Public Health (DrPH), Master of Public Health (MPH), Master of Science (MS) in Clinical Research, and Master of Professional Studies in Homeland Security with an option in Public Health Preparedness, as well as several graduate certificate programs. The successful candidate will provide leadership and oversight for the DrPH program, working collaboratively with PHS leadership, faculty, students, and education staff to support program quality, student success, and continued program development. Responsibilities will include coordinating program activities; supporting student recruitment, progression, and engagement; contributing to curriculum and program planning; monitoring program outcomes and assessment; supporting accreditation activities; and identifying opportunities to strengthen the DrPH program and student experience. The position will also contribute to research activities within PHS, including participation in collaborative research projects and initiatives aligned with the department’s mission and areas of expertise. Candidates with experience in public health practice, higher education, program leadership, research, government, healthcare, nonprofit organizations, or related settings are encouraged to apply. The successful candidate should possess a doctoral degree in public health or a related discipline and demonstrate experience leading or managing an academic, professional, or public health program. Strong organizational, leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills are required. Experience with program assessment, accreditation, graduate education, or public health research is preferred. The Penn State College of Medicine is located in Hershey, PA, near the state capital of Harrisburg, with convenient access to major metropolitan areas including Philadelphia, Baltimore, New York City, Washington, DC, and Pittsburgh. Harrisburg International Airport and AMTRAK are less than ten miles away. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Salary will be commensurate with experience and credentials. Applicants should submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, and contact information for three professional references.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
