    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/College-of-Medicine/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Dermatology_REQ_0000081751-1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Dermatology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The laboratory of Dr. Ryan Hobbs in the Penn State College of Medicine, Department of Dermatology, is seeking a full-time Postdoctoral Scholar to work on campus in Hershey, Pennsylvania. Research in the Hobbs Laboratory focuses on understanding how epithelial cells sense and respond to cellular, environmental, and inflammatory stress. Using skin keratinocytes as a primary model system, the laboratory investigates the molecular mechanisms that regulate epithelial survival, differentiation, cell adhesion, tissue repair, and disease development. Current projects integrate advanced light microscopy, cell and molecular biology, functional genomics, and drug-discovery approaches to identify pathways that control keratinocyte stress responses and to evaluate potential therapeutic modifiers of epithelial dysfunction. The successful applicant will lead research projects employing advanced fluorescence and live-cell microscopy techniques to investigate dynamic cellular and molecular processes in keratinocytes. The position will also involve the development and implementation of targeted and higher-throughput drug-discovery screening approaches, including assay optimization, compound testing, quantitative imaging, and validation of candidate therapeutic agents. Applicants should possess pronounced expertise in keratinocyte biology and a strong foundation in cellular and molecular biology. Demonstrated experience with mammalian cell culture, fluorescence microscopy, quantitative image analysis, biochemical assays, and molecular biology techniques is strongly preferred. Experience with advanced light microscopy, automated imaging, drug or small-molecule screening, three-dimensional epithelial culture models, primary cell culture, or mouse skin biology is desirable. Responsibilities •    Independently design, conduct, analyze, and interpret experiments related to assigned research projects. •    Apply advanced light microscopy approaches, including fluorescence, confocal, live-cell, and quantitative imaging techniques. •    Develop and execute drug-discovery and small-molecule screening assays using keratinocyte and epithelial model systems. •    Establish, optimize, and troubleshoot cellular, molecular, biochemical, and imaging-based experimental methods. •    Maintain and experimentally manipulate primary and immortalized keratinocyte cultures and other relevant epithelial model systems. •    Analyze microscopy, molecular, and functional screening data using appropriate quantitative and statistical approaches. •    Seek out new scientific resources and learn or develop new techniques as warranted by project needs. •    Maintain accurate and complete experimental records and contribute to laboratory data-management practices. •    Present scientific findings at laboratory meetings, departmental seminars, scientific conferences, and other professional venues. •    Prepare scientific manuscripts, abstracts, reports, and other research-related documents. •    Contribute to the development of grant applications and future research directions. •    Train and mentor graduate students, undergraduate students, and other laboratory personnel. •    Contribute positively to the overall laboratory environment and participate actively in scientific discussions and collaborative projects. •    Ensure that research is conducted in compliance with institutional policies, approved protocols, and laboratory safety guidelines. Qualifications •    A PhD in biomedical sciences, cell biology, molecular biology, biochemistry, pharmacology, cancer biology, dermatology, or a related discipline by the appointment start date. •    Demonstrated research experience in keratinocyte biology, epithelial cell biology, skin biology, or a closely related area. •    Strong technical knowledge of cellular and molecular biology methods. •    Experience with mammalian cell culture and standard molecular and biochemical techniques. •    Experience with fluorescence microscopy and quantitative analysis of microscopy data. •    Evidence of scientific productivity and the ability to communicate research findings effectively. •    Ability to work independently while contributing effectively to a collaborative research environment.     BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
