    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-Hazleton/Campus-Chief-Academic-Officer--CCAO-_REQ_0000077786-2": {
      "title": "Campus Chief Academic Officer (CCAO)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants .   POSITION SPECIFICS Penn State Hazleton invites applications and nominations for the position of Campus Chief Academic Officer (CCAO) to begin on or about November 1, 2026. The CCAO is a 48-week academic administrative appointment. The CCAO is the senior campus academic officer, responsible for providing leadership for academic and faculty affairs in an environment of shared governance and collaboration. The CCAO reports directly to the Regional Chancellor and acts on behalf of the Regional Chancellor in their absence, or as designated. This position also receives direction and support from the Dean of the University College and is accountable to them, along with the Regional Chancellor, for implementing curricular and faculty affairs initiatives driven by the College. As a key member of the campus leadership team, the CCAO collaborates with the leadership of a variety of departments such as Student Affairs, Enrollment Management, Information Technology, Strategic Communications, Development and Alumni Relations, Finance, etc. and engages, as appropriate, with advisory boards and external partners. The CCAO also collaborates with leadership in other units within the university to ensure that Penn State operates as one university, geographically distributed, creating clear, accessible, and consistent pathways for student success.  RESPONSIBILITIES: Specific responsibilities of the CCAO include: Faculty leadership – Develop and implement academic vision and strategy using current best practices, innovative solutions, and data-informed decisions. Lead faculty recruitment, mentoring, development, and evaluation; foster teaching and advising excellence and innovation; enhance resources to advance belonging and professional fulfillment; further efforts in grant writing and funding to support research and academic programs; facilitate community impact via faculty research and service; support belonging, inclusiveness, and fulfillment; and foster and participate in an environment of shared governance. Academic staff leadership – Lead professional staff (e.g., registrar, instructional designer) and academic support operations, (e.g., advising, career services as applicable, tutoring, and student disability resources); oversee staff recruitment, mentoring, development, evaluation; enhance resources to foster belonging and professional fulfillment; and foster innovation in academic support operations. Student engagement and success – Lead academic and career success advancement for students, from dual enrollment to first year through graduation, into careers and professional and graduate schools; steer and support student engagement and student experiential and high impact learning practices (first-year experience, global programs, undergraduate research, service learning, internships, peer mentoring, honors coursework, and capstone projects); partner with campus leadership on initiatives to increase student recruitment, retention, and persistence to graduation; and support continuous improvement of the overall student academic experience including advising. Academic program and curricular leadership – Direct academic program and curricular planning, administration, and assessment including interdisciplinary education and research; support investment in established programs and new program development to align degrees with student interest and workforce needs; partner with campus leadership on technology, facilities, space planning, equipment, and other resources to ensure excellence in teaching and learning, research and creative activity, service and community impact. Budget planning and cross-unit engagement – Develop and administer all budgets and resources for academic programs, faculty development, and student academic support; collaborate with campus leadership on fundraising and grant development advancement to enhance academics. Instruction – May teach up to 6 credits per year, depending on campus enrollment. Qualifications: A doctorate or terminal degree; a minimum of five years in higher education as a full-time faculty member with evidence of excellence in teaching, research or creative activity, and service; and academic leadership experience and knowledge. Candidates must meet the academic qualifications for a tenured faculty appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor at Penn State.  The most qualified applicants will show evidence of staying abreast of current and emerging trends in higher education, integrating them into their work practices and leadership; possessing extensive academic knowledge; and the ability to lead and serve in a comprehensive land-grant, public university with multiple campus locations. Prior experience in effectively communicating and collaborating with diverse internal and external constituents is required. Interested and qualified applicants from the Commonwealth Campuses are preferred. APPLICATION:                                                                              Applicants should submit a letter of application describing interest in the position and qualifications for the position, curriculum vitae, and the names, titles, telephone numbers, and email addresses of four professional references, with at least one being a current or past supervisor. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until an appointment is made. CAMPUS INFORMATION: As Pennsylvania’s sole land-grant institution and largest public university, Penn State is ranked as a top US public university and global institution – for academic standing, specialty programs, and research that impacts the world. Penn State Hazleton is a residential campus of Penn State, the land-grant University of the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, serving over 90,000 students. The beautiful, suburban campus is located on 125 acres overlooking the Conyngham Valley and is conveniently located near Interstates 80 and 81 in northeastern Pennsylvania. The campus has a long-standing history of academic excellence and regional leadership in higher education. Current enrollment is 605 full and part-time students from 20 states and 10 countries. One of Penn State's most diverse campuses, 45% of students are from diverse backgrounds. Thirteen baccalaureate degree programs range from engineering focused on alternative energy and power generation to computer science to business. The five associate degree programs feature physical therapist assistant and medical laboratory technology. Students may also complete the first two years of nearly all of Penn State's 275 baccalaureate degrees at the Hazleton campus and then transition to another Penn State campus to complete their studies (2+2 program). The full on-campus student experience features robust cocurricular programming and eight men's and women's athletics teams that compete in the PSUAC and USCAA. The campus has strong business and industry partnerships, including the highly impactful Hazleton LaunchBox ( https://hazleton.launchbox.psu.edu/ ) , a signature program of the Invent Penn State Initiative, a commonwealth-wide network to spur economic development, job creation, and student career success.      BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies. Due to the financial and fiduciary responsibilities of this position, successful completion of a credit history check will be required in addition to standard background checks. This position requires that you operate a motor vehicle as a part of your job duties. A valid driver’s license and successful completion of a motor vehicle records check will be required in addition to standard background checks.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar--Immunology--Microbiology----Toxicology--Grembi-Lab_REQ_0000080624-1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar- Immunology, Microbiology, & Toxicology, Grembi Lab",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Grembi Lab at Penn State University is seeking a Postdoctoral Scholar with expertise in immunology, microbiology, toxicology, or a related field to join our team studying the ecology of the human small intestine. Our work focuses on environmental enteropathy, a subclinical condition characterized by intestinal inflammation and increased permeability that is thought to contribute to childhood undernutrition and stunting. We use an interdisciplinary approach combining microbiology, immunology, biochemistry, computational biology, and epidemiology to understand how microbial communities in the small intestine develop, interact with the host, and respond to environmental conditions, with an increasing focus on environmental contaminants. Our team is based at Penn State's main campus in State College, Pennsylvania (a.k.a. Happy Valley), a welcoming college town with a remarkably low cost of living and easy access to outdoor recreation. Penn State's position as a leading R1 research university means you'll also have access to cutting-edge technology, a vibrant research community within the Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences and the One Health Microbiome Center, and numerous opportunities for local and global collaborations. Responsibilities The Postdoctoral Scholar will: Independently initiate, execute, and complete interdisciplinary research involving immunology, toxicology, molecular biology, and biochemistry Communicate research findings via presentations at conferences and peer-reviewed manuscripts Contribute to grant proposals and fellowship applications, gaining experience in research funding and scientific writing Mentor and train graduate and undergraduate students Qualifications Applicants should have a PhD in Immunology, Microbiology, Biology, Toxicology, Biochemistry, or a related field, along with excellent oral and written communication skills and at least one first-author publication. Strong candidates will have experience in at least two of the following areas: multiparameter flow cytometry; single-cell, RNA sequencing, or shotgun metagenomics data generation and analysis; intestinal organoids, primary human cells, or animal models of gut inflammation. Candidates should be highly motivated and creative, with a genuine interest in global health. What We Offer We are committed to building an inclusive and equitable lab environment and strongly encourage applications from candidates of all backgrounds. You will benefit from close mentorship from the PI and significant autonomy over your project. This position offers an excellent platform to develop skills in data science and statistics, with flexibility to tailor your training to align with your professional goals. Position Details Start date is flexible between September 2026 and January 2027. This is a limited-term position funded for one year with the potential to extend based on performance and funding. Applicants are required to have a Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate in an appropriate field and be able to provide evidence that all requirements have been met for completion of the Ph.D. prior to the effective date of hire. Application Process Interested candidates should submit an online application at Penn State's Job Posting Board , and should upload the following application materials electronically:      CV a recent manuscript they were a primary author on (preprints are fine) a brief statement of their research interests and how they envision pursuing those on the Grembi lab contact information for 2-3 professional references   System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-or-Associate-Clinical-Professor--Penn-State-Psychological-Clinic_REQ_0000081026-2": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor, Penn State Psychological Clinic",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Psychology at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a full-time adult-track, Assistant or Associate Clinical Professor position for the Penn State Psychological Clinic .  The Psychological Clinic is a fully licensed comprehensive outpatient community mental health center for the region, as well as the primary training and research site for the Ph.D. program in Clinical Psychology. The clinic is among the largest associated with a doctoral training program in the United States, providing psychological and neuropsychological assessment for adults, adolescents, and children; psychological outpatient treatment for adults,  adolescents, children, and families, and psychiatric outpatient treatment for adults, including those with serious mental illness and personality pathology; and school- and hospital-based intervention programs. Faculty supervisors and clinical staff are licensed and paneled with major insurance companies to bill for services.  Penn State is an APA and PCSAS accredited clinical science doctoral program. The Psychological Clinic facilitates the seamless integration of research and practice in clinical training with a fully developed practice-research network for conducting clinical investigations.  This clinical faculty appointment is a non-tenure-line position. We wish to fill this position immediately; start date is negotiable.   The College of the Liberal Arts is committed to offering professional growth and promotional opportunities for non-tenure-line faculty appointments.  Information on faculty ranks and progression can be found at  https://policy.psu.edu/policies/ac21 Responsibilities include direct clinical care (i.e., individual and group psychotherapy, assessment, consultation) in the Psychological Clinic and/or in community agencies contracted with the Clinic, as well as a combination of undergraduate/classroom teaching, graduate practicum teaching, and supervision of Clinical Psychology PhD students. This position will include resident and online instruction and normal university service.  MINIMUM EDUCATION, WORK EXPERIENCE & REQUIRED CERTIFICATIONS A Doctorate in Clinical or Counseling Psychology or related field is required by the appointment date, and the candidate must be licensed or license eligible within 90 days of hire. Rank and length of term are determined by qualifications. Experience with conducting assessments and providing evidence-based treatment is required; experience with one or more of the following is also strongly preferred: Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT), Psychodynamic Therapy/ies (e.g., Transference-Focused Therapy/TFP) and Dialectical Behavioral Therapy (DBT)). Other preferred qualifications include knowledge of HIPPA regulations and mental health law, an exceptional interest in the integration of science and practice, and a commitment to inclusion in the applicant’s clinical practice, teaching, and/or supervision. Interested candidates must submit an online application at  Penn State’s Job Posting Board, and should upload the following application materials: a letter of interest, CV or resume, and a list of three references with contact information.  For information or questions regarding the position, please contact Dr. Sandra Testa Michelson at smt3@psu.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/College-of-Medicine/Researcher---Medicine_REQ_0000080923-3": {
      "title": "Researcher - Medicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 18 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Penn State College of Medicine, Department of Medicine in Hershey, PA is seeking a non-tenure line Researcher. The Nighot laboratory has been focused on intestinal mucosal homeostasis in health and disease ( https://sites.psu.edu/nighot/ ). The lab is especially interested in the role of defective intestinal tight junction (TJ) barrier in inflammatory bowel disease (IBD), including Crohn’s Disease and ulcerative colitis, and the role of autophagy in TJ barrier regulation. Autophagy, a cell survival mechanism, degrades unnecessary, misfolded and long-lived proteins and organelles and helps cell survive under stress. The lab's pioneering studies have shown that autophagy enhances TJ barrier and ameliorates intestinal inflammation in experimental colitis. We are also interested in investigating novel targets to combat IBD, and the role of extra cellular matrix proteins, ion transporters, signaling molecules, and cytokines in intestinal inflammation. We have also recently begun investigating the role of autophagy and gut-liver axis in liver diseases. We use in-vivo ,  ex-vivo , whole animal, and  in-vitro  approaches in our research work. The techniques used in the lab include cell and molecular approaches, genetically modified animal models, advanced confocal imaging, flow cytometry, innovative culture models such as organoids, and working with clinical samples. The main responsibility of the person in this position is to actively participate in the ongoing research projects in the lab, explore new techniques and new direction of research, and provide support to the PI in developing research proposals. Ample professional and career development opportunities are available at the Penn State College of Medicine ( https://med.psu.edu /). Responsibilities Job duties include but are not limited to developing, designing and conducting research projects under general direction of the PI but in self-driven fashion; developing appropriate research methods; creative use of animal models; data analyses and interpretation; presentation of research in scientific conferences and meetings; and manuscript preparation. This is an appointment for one year from the date of hire; extension subjected to the availability of funds. Qualifications The successful candidate will have a PhD in cell and molecular biology or comparable field and experience in the related research field. The candidate will demonstrate evidence of strong research knowledge, skills and attitudes; an interest in the research field and a familiarity and success with the academic team research environment. The candidate will have ability for critical, out-of-box thinking, innovation in research work, ability to interrogate cellular pathways, and practical knowledge of advanced molecular techniques beside molecular cloning, site-directed mutagenesis, and genetic modulation. Candidates who have been highly productive with motivation and passion for science and a wide range of research experiences, including analysis of human datasets are encouraged to apply.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
