    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Director--The-Penn-State-Critical-Materials-Alliance_REQ_0000081293-1": {
      "title": "Director, The Penn State Critical Materials Alliance",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants .   POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University invites applications and nominations for the inaugural Director of the Penn State Critical Materials Alliance ( Penn State CMA) , a strategic university-wide initiative focused on advancing research, workforce development, industry engagement, and innovation across the critical minerals and materials value chain. Penn State possesses the breadth required to address the entire critical minerals and materials lifecycle - the new Director will be instrumental in aggregating and focusing expertise across campus .   The Penn State CMA is a university-wide initiative managed by the Materials Research Institute (MRI) on behalf of Penn State's Office of the Senior Vice President for Research. The Alliance brings together faculty and research infrastructure from across the University, including the Colleges of Earth and Mineral Sciences, Engineering, Eberly College of Science, Smeal College of Business, and Information Sciences and Technology, together with Penn State's Applied Research Laboratory (ARL) and major interdisciplinary institutes including the Institute of Energy and the Environment (IEE), National Security Institute (NSI), and Institute for Computational and Data Sciences (ICDS).   The Director will provide visionary leadership for a growing interdisciplinary effort spanning resource discovery and characterization, extraction and separation, advanced materials processing and manufacturing, circular economy approaches, artificial intelligence and supply-chain analytics, and the societal dimensions of critical minerals and materials development. The successful candidate will hold a tenured faculty appointment at the Professor rank in an academic department aligned with their expertise and will work closely with colleges, interdisciplinary institutes, and research centers across the University. Exceptionally accomplished candidates currently at the Associate Professor rank may be considered when their record supports appointment at the Professor rank.   The Director will be responsible for building and leading a nationally recognized interdisciplinary program that positions Penn State as a leader in securing domestic supply chains for critical minerals and materials essential to energy technologies, advanced manufacturing, national security, and economic competitiveness.   Responsibilities   The Director will be expected to :   • Develop and execute a strategic vision for the Penn State CMA .   • Build and lead interdisciplinary teams spanning multiple colleges, institutes, and campuses.   • Foster a collaborative culture that integrates expertise across exploration, extraction, processing, manufacturing, recycling, AI-enabled systems, economics, policy, and workforce development.   • Expand partnerships with industry, federal agencies, national laboratories, state agencies, and international collaborators.   • Develop and lead large-scale research initiatives and center-scale proposals to federal sponsors including DOE, DoD, USGS, NSF, NIST, and related agencies.   • Establish and grow industry partnerships, consortia, and collaborative research programs with Federal Labs ( e.g. DOE Labs) that accelerate technology translation and workforce development.   • Coordinate strategic investments in shared research infrastructure, pilot-scale testbeds, and workforce programs that support critical minerals and materials innovation.   • Advance educational and workforce initiatives that prepare students, postdoctoral scholars, and technical professionals for careers in the critical minerals and materials ecosystem.   • Serve as an advocate and spokesperson for Penn State's critical minerals and materials activities at the regional, national, and international levels.   • Maintain an internationally recognized program of scholarship consistent with appointment at the rank of Professor.   Director Resources   The successful candidate will receive a competitive salary and startup package commensurate with their experience and consistent with Penn State policies. In addition, Penn State is committed to providing the resources necessary to establish the Penn State Critical Materials Alliance as a nationally recognized center of excellence that convenes academia, industry, and government . This support will include the operational and programmatic infrastructure needed to foster interdisciplinary collaboration, develop strategic partnerships, and accelerate the growth of large-scale research and workforce initiatives. Resources will be provided through a collaborative investment involving the University, participating colleges, and interdisciplinary institutes, with the goal of establishing a sustainable, nationally recognized Alliance.   Required Qualifications   Candidates must possess :   • An earned doctorate in engineering, materials science, geosciences, chemistry, physics, or a closely related field.   • Qualifications commensurate with appointment as a tenured Professor at Penn State ; exceptionally accomplished Associate Professors may be considered when their record supports appointment at the Professor rank.   • An internationally recognized record of scholarship and research accomplishments relevant to critical minerals, materials, energy technologies, advanced manufacturing, resource systems, recycling, supply chains, or related fields.   • A demonstrated record of leading large interdisciplinary research programs, centers, institutes, consortia, or comparable collaborative efforts, with the stature and credibility to lead senior faculty across multiple academic units.   • Strong communication and relationship-building skills with academic, industry, government, and community stakeholders.   • Demonstrated commitment to fostering collaborative and inclusive research environments.   • US Citizen or Green Card Holder     Preferred Qualifications   Preference will be given to candidates with:   • Experience leading multi-institutional or center-scale research initiatives.   • Experience working with federal agencies and national laboratories.   • Experience developing industry partnerships and translational research programs.   • Knowledge of one or more areas relevant to the critical minerals and materials value chain, including exploration, extraction and separation, advanced manufacturing, circular economy and recycling, supply-chain resilience, artificial intelligence and digital systems.   • Experience building workforce development, educational, or training programs.     Applications should include a curriculum vitae, Research & Leadership Statement, and professional references .     About the Penn State Critical Materials Alliance ( Penn State CMA )   The Penn State CMA i s Penn State's university-wide organization for coordinating research, education, workforce development, industry engagement, and strategic partnerships in critical minerals and materials. Managed by the Materials Research Institute on behalf of the Office of the Senior Vice President for Research, the Alliance brings together faculty, facilities, and programs from across the University to address the entire critical minerals and materials value chain—from resource discovery and extraction to processing, advanced manufacturing, recycling, and supply-chain resilience.   The Penn State CMA serves as Penn State's focal point for interdisciplinary collaboration and external engagement, accelerating large-scale research initiatives, technology translation, workforce development, and partnerships with industry, federal agencies, national laboratories, and state organizations. By integrating expertise across the Colleges of Earth and Mineral Sciences, Engineering, Eberly College of Science, Information Sciences and Technology, Smeal College of Business, the Applied Research Laboratory, and major interdisciplinary institutes—including the Materials Research Institute (MRI), Institute of Energy and the Environment (IEE), National Security Institute (NSI), and Institute for Computational and Data Sciences (ICDS)—the Alliance positions Penn State as a national leader in advancing secure, sustainable, and resilient critical minerals and materials supply chains.     About Penn State   Penn State is a top-ranked public research university and one of the largest and most comprehensive universities in the United States. With more than $1. 4 billion in annual research expenditures and a longstanding commitment to interdisciplinary collaboration, Penn State provides an exceptional environment for research, innovation, education, and public impact.     BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-Position-in-Functional-Ceramic-Materials_REQ_0000080791-1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar Position in Functional Ceramic Materials",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for a Postdoctoral Scholar position in the area of functional ceramic materials in the Randall group. The successful candidate will join an internationally recognized research group conducting cutting-edge research on the processing, characterization, and performance of advanced ceramic materials for energy, electronic, and electromechanical applications within the Materials Research Institute (MRI), The research program focuses on a broad range of functional ceramics, including:  Piezoelectric and ferroelectric materials  Capacitor dielectric materials  Cathode materials for next-generation batteries  Advanced ceramic processing and microstructural engineering  The successful candidate should have demonstrated expertise in the processing, structure, property, and performance relationships of ceramic materials. Experience in one or more of the following areas is highly desirable:  Ceramic powder synthesis and processing  Structural and microstructural characterization  Scanning Electron Microscopy (SEM)  Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM)  Atomic Force Microscopy (AFM)  X-ray diffraction (XRD) and related X-ray characterization techniques  Electrical and electromechanical characterization of functional ceramics  Impedance spectroscopy  Electrochemical characterization  Thermally Stimulated Depolarization Current (TSDC) analysis  Ferroelectric, dielectric, piezoelectric, or electrochemical measurements  Other advanced characterization techniques relevant to functional materials  The Postdoctoral Scholar will be expected to:  Conduct independent, high-quality research leading to publications in leading international journals.  Develop and execute innovative research projects aligned with the group's research objectives.  Work collaboratively with graduate students, undergraduate researchers, visiting scientists, and faculty collaborators.  Provide technical guidance and mentorship to students and visiting researchers.  Assist with the operation and development of advanced experimental capabilities within the laboratory.  Contribute to the preparation of research proposals, technical reports, and presentations.  Present research findings at national and international conferences.  Publish research in high-level journals.  Required Qualifications:  Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Ceramic Engineering, Physics, Chemistry, or a closely related discipline.  Strong experimental background in functional ceramic materials.  Excellent written and oral communication skills.  Demonstrated publication record in peer-reviewed journals.  Ability to work both independently and as part of a multidisciplinary research team.  Preferred Qualifications and Experience in one or more of the following areas will be considered an advantage:  Functional oxide ceramics  Ferroelectric and piezoelectric materials  Multilayer ceramic capacitors (MLCCs)  Solid-state electrochemistry  Battery materials  Advanced microscopy and spectroscopy  Reliability and degradation of electronic materials  Data analysis and modeling of structure–property relationships  This position offers the opportunity to work within a highly collaborative and internationally recognized research environment with access to state-of-the-art characterization and processing facilities. The successful candidate will be encouraged to develop independent research directions while contributing to a broad portfolio of sponsored research programs.  Applications should include a cover letter describing research interests and relevant experience, a curriculum vitae, a list of publications, and the names and contact information of three professional references.    BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Cybersecurity-and-Privacy-Tenure-line-Faculty-Position_REQ_0000081189-1": {
      "title": "Cybersecurity and Privacy Tenure-line Faculty Position",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants .   POSITION SPECIFICS Cybersecurity and Privacy Tenure-line Faculty Position The Department of Privacy and Cybersecurity in the College of Information Sciences and Technology (IST) at The Pennsylvania State University invites applications for two tenure-line faculty positions in Cybersecurity and Privacy located in State College, Pennsylvania. The appointments are at the assistant or associate professor rank and begin in January of 2027 at the University Park campus. We seek outstanding scholars with expertise in one or more of the following areas :  the intersection of  artificial intelligence (AI), security, and privacy; organizational, behavioral, and/or human factors in cybersecurity and privacy; digital forensics and/or cyber investigations; systems and software security; cryptography; quantum computing and post-quantum security; or other emerging areas in cybersecurity, privacy, and/or trustworthy computing. We particularly welcome applicants whose research demonstrates interdisciplinary collaboration and addresses significant societal, governmental, or industrial challenges. Candidates will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in residential, online, and/or hybrid modes; conduct cutting-edge interdisciplinary research; supervise and mentor graduate students; actively pursue external funding to support research activities; engage in service activities at the college and university levels; and collaborate with faculty across the university and with industry partners. Candidates will possess a PhD in information science, computer science, cybersecurity, or a related field before their appointment start date at Penn State. Applicants for the rank of Assistant Professor will demonstrate strong potential for developing a collaborative, interdisciplinary research project that is competitive for external funding and potential to contribute to the college’s teaching mission. Candidates seeking the rank of Associate Professor should have the same as Assistant Professor and a strong record of scholarly achievement, external funding, and demonstrated success in teaching and service. How to apply: https://ist.psu.edu/PCI-Tenureline-Ad Applicants will attach documentation during their application process and should include a cover letter with information about their interests and qualifications for the position. They will also include a description of their i) research accomplishments and plans (2-3 pages), and ii) approach to teaching (1-2 pages). They provide the iii) applicant’s curriculum vitae and iv) contact information for at least three professional references. Applicants may combine their descriptions into one cover letter and combine all file(s) into one document prior to uploading, or they may upload separate files. Inquiries about the position may be directed to facultyrecruiting@ist.psu.edu . Review of applications begins on September 15, 2026, and will continue until positions are filled.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Reinhart-Group---Materials-Science-and-Engineering_REQ_0000081196-1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Reinhart Group - Materials Science and Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Materials Science and Engineering in the College of Earth and Mineral Sciences is searching for a postdoctoral scholar. The position will involve machine learning for autonomous thin-film materials synthesis, including representation learning for scientific data, multimodal data fusion, and real-time predictive modeling. This work will be performed as part of LATTICE (Layered and Thin Film Technologies with Intelligent Cloud Experimentation), a National Science Foundation Programmable Cloud Laboratory at the Pennsylvania State University’s University Park campus. The postdoctoral scholar will develop specialized machine learning models that enable AI systems to interpret scientific data from instruments including atomic force microscopy, reflection high-energy electron diffraction, spectroscopic ellipsometry, X-ray diffraction, and similar characterization methods. These models serve as the perceptual layer for a multi-agent AI framework that will guide autonomous materials synthesis and interact with robotic systems. The models will be trained, calibrated, and validated against the specific data modalities produced by LATTICE instrumentation. The scholar will deploy these models on edge-computing infrastructure for real-time feedback during deposition and integrate them with the Lifetime Sample Tracking data platform. The position requires close collaboration with LATTICE domain scientists in thin-film growth and characterization, AI researchers developing the agentic workflow framework, and future users of the LATTICE framework. Requirements Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Materials Science and Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Physics, or a related field, plus a strong record of research experience in applied machine learning, computer vision, and/or scientific data analysis. Preferred Experience with one or more of the following is strongly preferred: deep learning for image analysis, multimodal or multi-task learning, or deployment of ML models in real-time or edge-computing environments. Domain knowledge of materials science, chemistry, or physics will be an advantage. Extensive programming experience in Python is required, and familiarity with PyTorch or JAX is preferred.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/College-of-Medicine/Postdoctoral-Scholar---Cardiac-Electrophysiology-and-Arrhythmia-Research_REQ_0000080924-2": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar – Cardiac Electrophysiology and Arrhythmia Research",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS Postdoctoral Scholar – Cardiac Electrophysiology and Arrhythmia Research Department of Medicine –Penn State College of Medicine Hershey, Pennsylvania The laboratory of Dr. Mahmud Arif and Dr. Dawood Darbar in the Department of Medicine at Penn State College of Medicine is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Scholar to join a cardiovascular research program focused on the molecular and cellular mechanisms of cardiac arrhythmias. Our research integrates genetically engineered mouse models, cardiac electrophysiology, ion channel biology, and translational cardiovascular research to investigate how genetic variants and environmental risk factors contribute to cardiac arrhythmias and electrical remodeling. Research Areas The successful candidate will participate in projects involving: Mouse models of cardiac arrhythmias/sudden cardiac death Isolation and functional characterization of atrial and ventricular cardiomyocytes Cardiac electrophysiology and ion channel studies Molecular and cellular mechanisms of inherited arrhythmias Functional characterization of disease-associated genetic variants Development of novel therapeutic strategies for arrhythmia prevention and treatment Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Biology, Physiology, Pharmacology, Biomedical Sciences, Cardiovascular Sciences, Molecular Biology, or a related field Ph.D. completed within the last 1–2 years Demonstrated experience working with mouse models Expertise in mouse handling, breeding, genotyping, and animal procedures Proven experience isolating adult mouse atrial/ventricular cardiomyocytes, Langendorff perfusion method preferred. Strong publication record, including at least one first-author peer-reviewed publication Excellent written and verbal communication skills Ability to work independently while contributing effectively to a collaborative research environment Preferred Qualifications Experience with whole-cell patch-clamp electrophysiology Experience recording cardiac ionic currents and action potentials in isolated cardiomyocytes Knowledge of cardiac electrophysiology and arrhythmia mechanisms Experience with calcium imaging, optical mapping, or cardiac physiology techniques Familiarity with molecular biology techniques, including qPCR, Western blotting, RNA sequencing, and bioinformatics analysis Experience analyzing electrophysiological and omics datasets Career Development The successful candidate will receive strong mentorship and career development support from Dr. Mahmud Arif and Dr. Dawood Darbar. The laboratory is committed to helping postdoctoral scholars establish independent research careers through: Individualized mentoring and career planning Opportunities to lead research projects and publish in high-impact journals Guidance in developing fellowship applications and career development awards Encouragement and support for applying to NIH, AHA, and other external funding mechanisms Training in grant writing, scientific communication, and laboratory leadership Application Materials Interested applicants should submit: Cover letter describing research interests and career goals Curriculum vitae (CV) Contact information for three professional references Representative publications Penn State College of Medicine is committed to fostering an inclusive and collaborative research environment and welcomes applications from individuals with diverse backgrounds and experiences.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant--Associate--or-Full-Teaching-Professor--of-Companion-Animal-Biology-and-Management_REQ_0000080654-2": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Teaching Professor  of Companion Animal Biology and Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS Assistant, Associate, or Full Teaching Professor of Companion Animal Biology and Management JOB DESCRIPTION The Department of Animal Science at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park, invites applications for an Assistant, Associate, or Full Teaching Professor of Companion Animal Biology and Management. This is a 48-week, non-tenure line faculty position with 75% Teaching and 25% Extension responsibilities. The successful candidate will provide leadership in companion animal teaching and youth outreach programs and will play a central role in undergraduate education within the Animal Science major. Undergraduate teaching responsibilities may include ANSC 150S (ANSC Freshman Seminar), ANSC 215 (Pets in Society), ANSC 305 (Companion Animal Nutrition), ANSC 315 (Small Animal Health and Disease), ANSC 415 (Companion Animal Behavior), ANSC 419W (Applied Animal Welfare), and/or development of additional courses aligned with departmental needs and candidate expertise. Penn State values the incorporation of experiential learning into formal coursework. The faculty member will mentor undergraduate students and advise the Small and Exotic Animal Club. The successful candidate will develop and deliver Extension and outreach programs focused on companion animal science through activities such as 4-H/youth programs, workshops, camps, and educational events. They will collaborate with Penn State Extension personnel to deliver educational materials through in person and virtual formats and will engage with stakeholders, alumni, and companion animal organizations to support educational initiatives. The successful candidate will contribute to collaborative scholarship across the Department and College of Agricultural Sciences. They will engage in appropriate professional and service activities within and outside the Department. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE Applicants must have a Ph.D. and/or D.V.M/V.M.D. degree in Animal Science, Veterinary Medicine, or a closely related field. A D.V.M/V.M.D is preferred. Areas of expertise may include nutrition, physiology, reproduction, genetics, disease, behavior, or related disciplines. The successful candidate must have completed all degree requirements by the appointment date. Candidates must demonstrate excellence in teaching and effective outreach to formal and non-formal audiences. Experience with experiential learning, youth programs, or student organizations is desirable. Strong communication, teamwork, and leadership skills to work effectively with a diverse population of faculty, staff, students, youth audiences, and stakeholders are essential. APPLICATION Candidates should apply online with the following information: (1) cover letter, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) names and contact information for three references, and (4) a statement of teaching philosophy and interests.  The Department of Animal Science at Penn State includes 32 faculty members and is home to internationally recognized programs in animal nutrition, reproduction, physiology, and genetics. The companion animal curriculum is a rapidly growing program in the Department and provides extensive opportunities for student engagement, experiential learning, and outreach. The successful candidate will join a collaborative faculty committed to excellence in teaching, advising, and student success.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
